# ─── Supabase — required to run `npm run dev` ─────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in real values from the
# Supabase project: Project Settings → API.
#
# Only these two are read by the Next.js app (src/lib/supabase.ts,
# src/app/resultados/page.tsx) — verified by grepping src/ for process.env.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars are exposed to the browser; that's expected for the anon key.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...anon-key...

# ─── Not needed for `npm run dev` ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are consumed by the Supabase Edge Function (supabase/functions/), which
# has its own .env at supabase/functions/.env and its own dev/deploy flow — not
# part of running the Next.js app. Listed here only because some earlier setups
# put all five in one .env.local; keep them if you also work on the Edge
# Function locally, otherwise the two NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars above are all you need.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...anon-key...
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...service-role-key...
